🤖 [Qwen Edge] To connect to your MongoDB cluster using PHP, you can use the `MongoDB` extension in PHP which provides access to a MongoDB server.
Here is an example of connecting to a cluster with multiple servers:
```php
$cluster = new \MongoDB\Cluster("mongodb://localhost:27017", [
  'replicaSet' => 'rs0',
]);

foreach ($cluster->getServerList() as $server) {
  echo "Connecting to {$server->host}:{$server->port}...\n";

  // Connect to the server
  $db = new \MongoDB\Database($cluster, 'your_database_name');

  // Now you can use methods like `$db->collection('collection_name')->findOne()` to interact with the database.
}
```

In this example, replace `'localhost:27017'` and `'rs0'` with your actual MongoDB cluster details. Replace `'your_database_name'` with the name of the database you want to connect to in the cluster.
Also, make sure that the PHP extension for MongoDB is installed on your server or local machine. You can install it using `pecl install mongodb`.
Note: Be aware that connection timeout errors could occur due to network issues. To handle this scenario, consider implementing a mechanism such as retrying connections if an error occurs.

